# todo.nvim

A simple To-do plugin for Neovim for each project and preview as Markdown

## Installation

```lua
-- lazy.nvim
{
    'TimothyGCY/todo.nvim',
    config = function()
        require('todo')
    end
}
```

## Features

#### 1. User Commands

- TodoList

> Open a new tab and list all the todos of current project

- TodoAdd

> Create a new entry of todo, `:TodoAdd foo bar`

#### 2. Keymaps

| Keymap | Function |
| - | - |
| `` | Toggle todo/task completion |
| `dd` | Delete todo |
| `a` | Create a new entry of todo |
| `e` | Modify todo's description |
| `r` | Reload todo list |
| `q` | Close todo list |

---

> **Note**
This plugin will create a local file `.nvim_todo.json` to the project's root directory, you might want to include this file to your `.gitignore`, based on your preference.

